    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for juvenile myelomonocytic leukaemia</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "M. Tarek Elghetany",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 707.1pt; background: #daeef3; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"943\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical, haematological, and laboratory criteria (all five criteria are required):</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Peripheral blood monocyte count &ge;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/L</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Blast and promonocyte percentage of &lt;&nbsp;20% in peripheral blood and bone marrow</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical evidence of organ infiltration, most commonly splenomegaly</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No Philadelphia (Ph) chromosome or <em>BCR</em>::<em>ABL1 </em>fusion</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No <em>KMT2A </em>(<em>MLL1</em>) gene rearrangement</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Genetic criteria (one criterion is required):</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 4pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mutation in a component or a regulator of the canonical RAS pathway:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 72pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span class=\"TableTextChar\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: 'Courier New';\">o<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clonal <span class=\"TableTextChar\">somatic mutation in <em>PTPN11</em>, <em>KRAS</em>, or <em>NRAS</em><sup>a</sup>, <strong>or</strong></span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 72pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: 'Courier New';\">o<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clonal somatic or germline <em>NF1 </em>mutation and loss of heterozygosity or compound heterozygosity of <em>NF1</em>, <strong>or</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 72pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: 'Courier New';\">o<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clonal somatic or germline <em>CBL </em>mutation and loss of heterozygosity of <em>CBL</em><sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Non-canonical clonal RAS pathway pathogenic variant<sup>c</sup> or fusions causing activation of genes upstream of the RAS pathway, such as <em>ALK</em>, <em>PDGFRB</em>, and <em>ROS1</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Other criteria:</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cases that do not meet any of the genetic criteria listed above (or for which genetic testing is not available) must meet at least two of the following criteria in addition to the aforementioned clinical, haematological, and laboratory criteria:</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Increased haemoglobin&nbsp;F for age</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Myeloid (promyelocytes, myelocytes, metamyelocytes) and erythroid precursors on peripheral blood smear</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Thrombocytopenia with hypercellular marrow often showing a decreased number of megakaryocytes; dysplastic features may or may not be evident</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.2pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hypersensitivity of myeloid progenitors to GM-CSF as tested in clonogenic assays in methylcellulose or by measuring STAT5 phosphorylation in the absence of or with a low dose of exogenous GM-CSF</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">GM-CSF, granulocyte&ndash;macrophage colony&ndash;stimulating factor.</span></p>\r\n<p><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">Germline</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"> mutation in <em>PTPN11</em>, <em>KRAS</em>, and <em>NRAS</em> (RASopathies resulting in Noonan syndrome) may produce juvenile myelomonocytic leukaemia&ndash;like transient myeloproliferative disorder. <sup>b</sup>Occasional cases have heterozygous splice-site mutations. <sup>c</sup>For example, <em>RRAS</em> or <em>RRAS2</em>.</span></p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
