    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Patient manifesting with JMML compatible clinical and haematological picture</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Absent <em>BCR</em>::<em>ABL1</em> fusion gene and <em>KMT2A</em> gene rearrangement</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 45.6pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 45.6pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Detection of a molecular pathogenic lesion in leukaemic cells in one of the five canonical RAS pathway driver genes in leukaemic cells (&gt;&nbsp;90% of JMML cases are defined by these molecular alterations):</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Biallelic pathogenic alterations of <em>NF1</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pathogenic <em>PTPN11</em> variant</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pathogenic <em>NRAS</em> variant</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pathogenic <em>KRAS</em> variant</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Biallelic pathogenic (in some cases heterozygous only) variants involving the <em>CBL</em> gene</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 59.4pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 59.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">OR</span></strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> detection of a non-canonical genetic abnormality:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Fusions leading to upstream RAS pathway activation (<em>ALK</em>, <em>PDGFRB</em>, and others)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Pathogenic variant in a non-canonical RAS pathway (<em>RRAS</em> or <em>RRAS2</em>) variant</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 106.8pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 106.8pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">In the absence of any of these alterations (or if molecular analysis is not possible):</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Performing additional laboratory studies as outlined in <span class=\"ID-File\">&lt;&lt;#32433&gt;&gt;</span>Box&nbsp;2.12</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Exclusion of conditions mimicking JMML, such as viral infection </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{11990701; 21571368}</span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">, infantile malignant osteopetrosis, and Wiskott&ndash;Aldrich syndrome</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 72.0pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Courier New'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Courier New';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">o<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">If monosomy&nbsp;7 is detected, elimination of syndromes commonly associated with this cytogenetic abnormality, such as <em>GATA2</em>-associated, <em>SAMD9</em>-associated, or <em>SAMD9L</em>-associated disorders</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
